@endnode


@node "intro" "Introduction"

@{u}@{b}Introduction@{ub}@{uu}

xircomce2.device is a SANA-II network driver for Xircom CreditCard Ethernet
PC Cards. These are sold by several companies under a variety of model
names; see below for (probable) compatibility.

Both 10 and 100 Mbps link speeds are supported, but achievable throughput is
approximately the same for each link speed, even with a fast CPU.
Autonegotiation of link speed and duplex mode are supported for cards that
have this feature.

@{u}@{b}Card Compatibility@{ub}@{uu}

The table below shows compatibility information for all known 16-bit
Ethernet and Ethernet/modem cards that have a Xircom chipset.

@{b}@{u}Company@{uu}		@{u}Model@{uu}		@{u}Works@{uu}	@{u}Notes@{uu}@{ub}

@{b}Accton@{ub}		EN2226		Maybe

@{b}Compaq@{ub}		335511-001	Yes
		335511-003	Maybe

@{b}Intel@{ub}		MBLA1600	Maybe
		MBLA1656	Maybe

@{b}NEC@{ub}		PS-CE2-10BC	Maybe

@{b}Xircom@{ub}		CE10		No	Older chipset
		CEM-10		No	Older chipset
		CEM-10BT	No	Older chipset
		CE-10/A		No	Older chipset
		CEM2		No	Older chipset
		PS-CE2-10	Yes
		PS-CEM28	No	Freezes system
		PS-CEM33	No	Freezes system
		CE3-10BC	Maybe
		CE3-10BT	Maybe
		CE3-10/100	Yes
		CE3B-100	Yes
		CE3B-100BTX	Yes
		RE-10BT		Maybe	Type III card
		XE2000		Yes	Type III card
		RE-100		Yes	Type III card
		RE-100BTX	Yes	Type III card
		CEM56-100	Yes
		REM56G-10BC	Yes	Type III card
		REM56G-10BT	Yes	Type III card
		REM56G-100BC	Yes	Type III card
		REM56G-100BTX	Yes	Type III card
		XEM5600		Yes	Type III card
		R2E-100BTX	Maybe	Type III card
		CFE-10		No	CF card with NE2000 chipset

In summary, the most suitable cards are those with model codes beginning
with CEM56 or CE3. Cards that have @{i}Yes@{ui} in the Works column above have been
tested with at least one A600 and A1200 motherboard revision.

Cards that have @{i}Maybe@{ui} in the Works column are very likely to work. Please
send a note if you test one of them so that the table can be updated.

Cards noted as Type III above will not fit into an A600 or A1200 desktop
case. They may fit in a tower system, although some right-angle adapters
only accommodate them with a very tight fit.

@endnode


@node "install" "Installation and Usage"

@{u}@{b}Requirements@{ub}@{uu}

xircomce2.device needs an A600 or A1200 and OS 2.05 or greater.

@{u}@{b}Installation@{ub}@{uu}

To install xircomce2.device, run the 'Install' script. In your networking
software, set the SANA-II device name to @{b}networks/xircomce2.device@{ub} and the
unit number to @{b}0@{ub}.

@{u}@{b}Cable types@{ub}@{uu}

Although some Xircom cards support @{"10base2" link "cable"} cabling, xircomce2.device
only supports @{"10baseT/100baseTX" link "cable"} cabling.

@{u}@{b}Multifunction cards@{ub}@{uu}

Although xircomce2.device works with some multifunction Ethernet/modem
cards, only one of these functions can be used at a time. This is due to
limitations in AmigaOS's card.resource. It is also uncertain if AmigaOS PC
Card serial/modem drivers will work with the modem function.

@{u}@{b}A1200 hardware bug@{ub}@{uu}

The A1200 (but not the A600) has a hardware bug that sometimes prevents a
card being reset. There are both software and hardware remedies for this
problem. The software solution is to use CardReset (util/boot/CardReset.lha
on Aminet) and CardPatch (util/boot/CardPatch.lha on Aminet). There are
several different types of hardware fixes, some of which may be available
commercially. Without using one of these solutions, you may experience
erratic behaviour with PC Cards.

@{u}@{b}Dongles@{ub}@{uu}

With the original dongle for your card, link and activity LEDs should work.
The link LED indicates when a connection has been established with the link
partner, e.g. your network switch or router. It glows green for a 10 Mbps
connection and orange for a 100 Mbps connection. The activity LED glows when
network traffic is flowing.

Older Xircom dongles bundled with 10 Mbps cards also work at 100 Mbps with
10/100 Mbps cards, but the link LED will not function when a 100 Mbps link
is established. Also note that the LEDs on compatible third-party dongles
may not function.

If you have trouble establishing a network link, make sure that you are
using a compatible dongle. Although several types of dongle may fit the
connector on the card perfectly, this does not mean that they are
necessarily compatible with the card.

Even some Xircom dongles are fussy about which cards they work with. E.g.
the "170-0458-003 A" dongle does not work with all cards.

@{u}@{b}Problems@{ub}@{uu}

With some A1200 motherboards, hot insertion or removal of a PC Card may
cause the system to reset.

Miami will cause the system to hang if the card is removed while online.
Re-insertion won't help.

@endnode


